format: 2
name: a JulcArray record component is rejected (#298)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 9f0102ff
expect: REJECT JULC0091
note: ADR-068 D6 (#298): a native array has no Data encoding, so a record holding one compiled and failed as soon
note: as the record was constructed (MkCons: element type ProtoArray does not match Data), where the JVM returns 2.
note: Under D4 exception 2 both frontends reject it at M1; recorded.base is the reference frontend at B0.
recorded.jvm: Value 02 []
recorded.base: Failure [] "MkCons: element type Apply[f=ProtoArray[], arg=Data[]] does not match list element type Data[]"
---
import java.math.BigInteger;
import org.julclang.core.types.JulcArray;
import org.julclang.core.types.JulcList;

public class Probe {
    record R(JulcArray<BigInteger> arr) {}

    public static BigInteger m(JulcList<BigInteger> xs) {
        R r = new R(xs.toArray());
        return BigInteger.valueOf(r.arr().length());
    }
}
